ast, us-west, eu-west). It is healthy, with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc is unhealthy in staging only.\n- **First attempt failed:** The rollback halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed across versions. I retried the same rollback once, and it completed in all regions. No policy approval was needed because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, \"checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0.\" The first create call timed out, so I checked the incident list before anything else. INC-0001 was already there, so there is no duplicate. Its summary describes the rollback, the partial failure, and the retry.\n\nStill open: root-cause the v2.3.1 health check failures, look into the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback, and confirm checkout traffic and revenue have recovered.", "type": "text"}]}]}